Found by the coordinator testing v0.4.0 from the marketplace (temp HOME): `skilletor add Getty/karr` stores source "getty" (git https://github.com/Getty/karr); a following `skilletor add Getty` stores "getty" = https://github.com/Getty/skills and karr is gone, no message. config.addSource does sources[name] = def, so re-adding also drops a ref pin or a local override on an existing entry.

Two fixes (decided by the coordinator):
1. add never replaces a source. If the target config already has a source by that name: same backend and address -> keep the entry as it is (ref, local and other fields stay), still trust and sync (idempotent re-add); a different address -> error, exit 1, config untouched, naming the existing address and the fix (pass a name: `skilletor add <name> <spec>`, or `skilletor source remove <name>` first). Only the file add writes to is checked.
2. Derived name: a git spec that names a repo other than the default `skills` derives the repo name (normalized, .git stripped), not the owner: Getty/karr -> karr, obra/superpowers -> superpowers, github:Getty/karr, gitlab.com/u/tools, https://github.com/Getty/karr(.git), git@github.com:Getty/karr.git -> repo name. Getty, anthropics, github.com/u, gitlab.com/u/skills, https://github.com/Getty/skills -> owner, as now. Generic probed hosts and url/local unchanged. Existing configs keep their names (names are stored).

Done when: tests red first for both; spec §4.2, README (Sources table/examples, and wherever a derived name is shown), skills/skilletor/SKILL.md updated; dist rebuilt; typecheck, npm test, build, check-dist green; hand test in a temp HOME with a ~/.claude dir: add Getty/karr then add Getty gives two sources karr and getty; add Getty/karr again keeps a ref you set by hand; add <name-of-existing> <other address> fails with exit 1 and leaves the file byte-identical.

